  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 18,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.848,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What are the other angles of the rhombus ABCD that we have constructed? Reason and/or experiment to figure this out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.141,
            0.806,
            0.16
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Deduction 9— What can we say about the angles in a rhombus?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.171,
            0.424,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider a rhombus GAME."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.19,
            0.44,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { G A E } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "GE = GA , a = d."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.208,
            0.503,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { M A E } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{ME} = \\mathrm{MA},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b = c ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.248,
            0.504,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It can be seen that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  GAE \\cong \\Delta  MAE"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (How?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.509,
            0.164,
            0.845,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.509,
                0.164,
                0.845,
                0.299
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.291,
            0.504,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = b , c = d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle G = \\angle M"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (since"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.31,
            0.67,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "they are corresponding parts of congruent triangles)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.329,
            0.422,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, we have, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = b = c = d."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.347,
            0.848,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These facts hold for any rhombus. Let us apply them to the rhombus ABCD that we constructed earlier. Let the four equal angles formed by the diagonal be a, as shown in the figure"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.437,
            0.355,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A D B } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.462,
            0.338,
            0.48
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "a+a+50=180^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.486,
            0.286,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 6 5 ^ { \\circ } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.407,
            0.682,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.37,
                0.407,
                0.682,
                0.531
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_15.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.54,
            0.57,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the angles of the rhombus ABCD are 50°, 130°, 50°, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.577,
            0.569,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in a rhombus opposite angles are equal to each other.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.619,
            0.57,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Interestingly, there is one more way by which we could have figured out the other angles of the rhombus ABCD. We have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.577,
            0.537,
            0.897,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 19,
              "bbox": [
                0.577,
                0.537,
                0.897,
                0.666
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_19.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.673,
            0.848,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "shown that in a general rhombus GAME, the four angles formed by a diagonal are equal to each other."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.712,
            0.48,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 21,
              "bbox": [
                0.162,
                0.712,
                0.48,
                0.835
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_21.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.841,
            0.52,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the lines EM and GA and its transversal AE. Since the alternate angles are equal, EM||GA."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.56,
            0.71,
            0.879,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 23,
              "bbox": [
                0.56,
                0.71,
                0.879,
                0.835
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_23.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.551,
            0.841,
            0.886,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly consider the lines GE and AM and its transversal AE. Since the alternate angles are equal, GE||AM."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
